  "historical_output_text": " Include tips for how to make the dish more flavorful or modify it for dietary restrictions. Consider using descriptive language to help the reader envision the dish.\n\nInstructions for a Simple Weeknight Meal - Grilled Chicken and Vegetable Skewers\n\nHeat a grill or grill pan over medium-high heat. While the grill is heating, prepare 12-16 wooden skewers. Thread 3-4 small pieces of chicken breast (1/2 inch thick) onto each skewer. Alternate with 2-3 slices of zucchini or yellow squash, 2-3 pieces of bell pepper (any color), and 2-3 cherry tomatoes. \n\nDrizzle the skewers with 2 tablespoons of olive oil and sprinkle with 1/2 teaspoon salt and 1/4 teaspoon freshly ground black pepper. Toss to coat the chicken and veggies evenly.\n\nPlace the skewers on the hot grill, skin side down for the chicken. Close the lid and grill for 6-8 minutes, or until the chicken is cooked through and no longer pink in the center. Rotate the skewers halfway through cooking. The veggies will be tender when a fork can easily pier",
